  "question": {
    "text": "The correct statement about the magnetic properties of \\(\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}\\) and \\(\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_6\\right]^{3-}\\) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "34Gy8",
      "text": "Both are paramagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "I2Kpv",
      "text": "Both are diamagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "kHSOy",
      "text": "\\(\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}\\) is diamagnetic, \\(\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_6\\right]^{3-}\\) is paramagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rdBkt",
      "text": "\\(\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}\\) is paramagnetic, \\(\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_6\\right]^{3-}\\) is diamagnetic",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(\\mathrm{Fe}^{+3}=[\\mathrm{Ar}] 3 \\mathrm{~d}^5 4 \\mathrm{~s}^0\\)\nFor \\(\\left[\\mathrm{Fe}(\\mathrm{CN})_6\\right]^{3-}\\)\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/mcTaiB2qxFfovS6oaQnnQ56ArFZEecESrtnfCaH7qtY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nPairing of \\(\\mathrm{e}^{-}\\)takes place as \\(\\mathrm{CN}^{-}\\)is strong field ligand but has one unpaired electron thus paramagnetic.\nFor \\(\\left[\\mathrm{FeF}_6\\right]^{-3}\\)\nAs \\(\\mathrm{F}^{\\text {- }}\\) is weak field ligand, so no pairing of electron, thus it has five unpaired electron. Therefore paramagnetic.",
    "image": null
  },
